versities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-6440d44d-1bf4-402d-8e58-767111cbebe7","sdu-9188c5e7-63cb-4175-9472-a0ecc56e2f10"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The Adverse Effects Associated With Ibuprofen Use After Major Orthopaedic Surgeries - A Detailed Statistical Analysis Plan for the PERISAFE Randomized Clinical Trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-087.50-813367","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: Non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs (NSAIDs) are recommended for pain treatment after elective hip and knee arthroplasties. However, evidence regarding the incidence of adverse effects with short-term NSAID treatment following surgery is limited. We, therefore, aim to assess the adverse effects with an eight-day postoperative treatment with ibuprofen after elective hip and knee arthroplasties. METHODS AND ANALYSIS: PERISAFE is a randomized, placebo-controlled, blinded multicenter trial with 90-day and one-year follow-up. Eligible patients undergoing elective hip or knee arthroplasty are allocated 1:1 to either ibuprofen 400 mg ×3/day or identical placebo ×3/day for eight days after surgery. The primary outcome is a composite of either death, acute myocardial infarction, stroke, pulmonary embolism, deep venous thrombosis, renal failure, major bleeding, re-operation, gastrointestinal ulcer, or readmission within 90 days postoperatively. Secondary outcomes are hospital-free days within 90 days postoperatively, a composite of ibuprofen and opioid-related adverse reactions based on eight-day postoperative diary, and health related quality of life after 90 days postoperatively. A total of 2904 patients are needed to demonstrate a relative risk reduction of 33% in the placebo group, accepting a risk of type I error of 5% and type II error of 20% and a proportion of serious adverse events in the ibuprofen group of 8%. The primary analysis will be in the modified intention-to-treat population. ETHICS AND DISSEMINATION: The trial is approved by the Danish Medicine Agency and the Research Ethics Committee (EU CT no. 2022-502, 502-32-00). We plan to submit for publication in a major international peer-reviewed journal and present results at scientific meetings.","author_count":24,"contributors":["Laursen, Christina Cleveland Westerdahl","Lunn, Troels Haxholdt","Hägi-Pedersen, Daniel","Therkelsen, Anne Sofie Nautrup","Varnum, Claus","Lange, Kai Henrik Wiborg","Yilmaz, Müjgan","Pedersen, Niels Anker","Kappel, Andreas","Jakobsen, Thomas","Eljaja, Salamah Belal","Thougaard, Thomas","Graungaard, Ben Kristian","Bjerno, Thomas","Beck, Jacob","Runge, Charlotte","Steiness, Joakim","Gasbjerg, Kasper Smidt","Thybo, Kasper Højgaard","Brorson, Stig","Lindberg-Larsen, Martin","Overgaard, Søren","Jakobsen, Janus Christian","Mathiesen, Ole"],"cuid":["S03-086.04-792763"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Laursen, Christina Cleveland Westerdahl"],"keyword":["Adverse effects","Anti Inflammatory Agents Non Steroidal therapeutic use","Arthroplasty","Arthroplasty Replacement Hip","Arthroplasty Replacement Knee","Double Blind Method","Hip arthroplasty","Humans","Ibuprofen","Ibuprofen therapeutic use","Knee arthroplasty","NSAID","Pain Postoperative drug therapy","Pain treatment","Postoperative Complications epidemiology","Randomized Controlled Trials as Topic","analgesic treatment","total hip arthroplasty surgery","total knee arthroplasty surgery","unicompartment knee arthroplasty"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Embargoed Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Capio Gildhøj Private Hospital"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the adverse effects with ibuprofen after major orthopedic surgeries a protocol for the perisafe randomized clinical trial","src":["aau","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85216650191&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The PERISAFE trial has received grants from Sygesikring \\u201Cdanmark,\\u201D The Independent Research Fund Denmark, the Zealand Region, the Danish Medical Associations Research Fund, and by Skibsreder Per Henriksen, R. og Hustrus fund. The funding sources have no influence on trial design and will have no influences on data collection, analysis, or reporting."],"id":"S03-086.04-792763","identifier":[{"id":"39887674","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85216650191","type":"scopus"},{"id":"001408864300001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-05d84a4f-dd81-4eb8-bf1f-4cc4824e5104","ku-7cf01493-e179-4b5e-b23e-813a53320dfd","sdu-925b5685-305a-4bd6-bb63-2ab6a0fe008b"],"keyword":["Anti-Inflammatory Agents, Non-Steroidal/therapeutic use","Arthroplasty, Replacement, Hip","Arthroplasty, Replacement, Knee","Double-Blind Method","Humans","Ibuprofen/therapeutic use","Pain, Postoperative/drug therapy","Postoperative Complications/epidemiology","Randomized Controlled Trials as Topic","adverse effects","analgesic treatment","arthroplasty","hip arthroplasty","ibuprofen","knee arthroplasty","nsaid","pain treatment","total hip arthroplasty surgery","total knee arthroplasty surgery","unicompartment knee arthroplasty"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-2EAF11F3012F171A4402C88D7B38943C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"ea","embargo":"2026-03-01","type":"loc","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"ea","embargo":"2027-01-30","type":"loc","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenha